        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "4501b63a-3d63-3644-815c-15865899ad21",
                "word": "autofiction",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "665c2141-7f44-452a-b778-236770a95b62",
                        "entry_id": "4501b63a-3d63-3644-815c-15865899ad21",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "autofictions"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "b60bafa3-9d04-49bc-bd04-1ffb4c246057",
                        "entry_id": "4501b63a-3d63-3644-815c-15865899ad21",
                        "tags": [
                            "rare"
                        ],
                        "form": "auto-fiction"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4dc9d8c1-628a-38aa-9e51-9c87cab9551b",
                        "entry_id": "4501b63a-3d63-3644-815c-15865899ad21",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Genre de roman où l’auteur s'inspire fortement de sa propre vie, pouvant confiner à l’autobiographie romancée."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "12b31752-cbd5-4cb7-aed7-b4bf7a0f3779",
                                "sense_id": "4dc9d8c1-628a-38aa-9e51-9c87cab9551b",
                                "text": "Il n’y a presque plus de romans, beaucoup d’autofictions, de biopics, de faits-divers transformés en livres."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9db0843c-0520-4744-8007-e0cf43b13366",
                                "sense_id": "4dc9d8c1-628a-38aa-9e51-9c87cab9551b",
                                "text": "Depuis le triomphe de l'autofiction, le texte narcissique, égotiste, contribue à la fabrication de vedettes parisiennes du monde des lettres."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ed7c6367-3253-4433-b0be-7f26854e5a50",
                                "sense_id": "4dc9d8c1-628a-38aa-9e51-9c87cab9551b",
                                "text": "Au vrai le terme d’autofiction ne m’évoquait que des idées imprécises, je l’avais mémorisé à l’occasion de la lecture d’un livre de Christine Angot (enfin des cinq premières pages), toujours est-il qu’en approchant des quais il me sembla de plus en plus que le mot convenait à ma situation, qu’il avait même été inventé pour moi […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a4dd50b6-07a0-453b-9de8-48a6cc7e61e1",
                                "sense_id": "4dc9d8c1-628a-38aa-9e51-9c87cab9551b",
                                "text": "« C’est le réflexe qu'on a, quand on parle d’autofiction, d’insister plus sur le auto que la fiction, mais pour moi ils sont égaux. »"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6a90f96f-0615-425a-b77a-f3891b05bb9b",
                                "sense_id": "4dc9d8c1-628a-38aa-9e51-9c87cab9551b",
                                "text": "On nomme « autofiction » des récits rédigés au présent et à la première personne du singulier dans lesquels l’écrivain se met en scène et se sent libre de tout dire, sa vie intime devenant vie publique."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5332107b-6cfd-49d2-a69c-ec5bd03b18df",
                                "sense_id": "4dc9d8c1-628a-38aa-9e51-9c87cab9551b",
                                "text": "Dans ce cas-ci comme dans plusieurs autres romans de Hesse, il s'agit bien, comme il l'a caractérisé lui-même, de Seelenbiographien (de « biographies de l'âme »), ancêtre des romans d’autofiction contemporains."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "fd73eb21-60a2-4426-9e73-a7d76ca82aad",
                        "source_entry_id": "4501b63a-3d63-3644-815c-15865899ad21",
                        "source_sense_id": "4dc9d8c1-628a-38aa-9e51-9c87cab9551b",
                        "source_sense_description": "Genre littéraire",
                        "target_lang_word": "Faction-Literatur",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e9f1a12f-b28d-4ffa-9096-777d1e64cdda",
                        "source_entry_id": "4501b63a-3d63-3644-815c-15865899ad21",
                        "source_sense_id": "4dc9d8c1-628a-38aa-9e51-9c87cab9551b",
                        "source_sense_description": "Genre littéraire",
                        "target_lang_word": "faction",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "faction",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5cf79eed-9a8d-31ee-a1ab-5b306d14dc4d",
                                        "entry_id": "d14bc415-b0ff-3ae5-baf3-8c108e50559a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A group of people, especially within a political organization, which expresses a shared belief or opinion different from people who are not part of the group."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cf3c4cf0-e568-4795-a5ea-4168daa08d59",
                                                "sense_id": "5cf79eed-9a8d-31ee-a1ab-5b306d14dc4d",
                                                "text": "Real factions may be divided into those from interest, from principle, and from affection"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "712183ea-8efa-43f5-807c-93c14d6bc1b2",
                                                "sense_id": "5cf79eed-9a8d-31ee-a1ab-5b306d14dc4d",
                                                "text": "Prejudice has bred a counterprejudice so that now neither faction can nor will see without distortion."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ea585313-f37f-4ed6-845d-0de6278f9afa",
                                                "sense_id": "5cf79eed-9a8d-31ee-a1ab-5b306d14dc4d",
                                                "text": "The Chinese Communist army in Kiangsi province has split into two factions struggling against each other following the purge of the \"gang of four\" led by Chiang Ching, according to an intelligence report from the Chinese mainland."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f6941886-3e6f-37a9-9c4b-c04e003a4535",
                                        "entry_id": "d14bc415-b0ff-3ae5-baf3-8c108e50559a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Strife; discord."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fd6a0f34-26a9-4037-b24f-b3edb0820576",
                                                "sense_id": "f6941886-3e6f-37a9-9c4b-c04e003a4535",
                                                "text": "Publick [sic] affairs soon fell into the utmost confusion, and in this state of faction and perplexity, the island continued, until its re-capture by the French in 1779."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "af86e353-8294-42ac-b014-ce5a5c019251",
                                                "sense_id": "f6941886-3e6f-37a9-9c4b-c04e003a4535",
                                                "text": "He asks the audience if they believe that they will be more loved by the gods if the city is in a state of faction than if they govern the city with good order and concord."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "faction",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d7a16fd6-b7e6-3312-b445-195b0bd39a44",
                                        "entry_id": "30c4bd1c-2952-39bf-93b6-37f4e4fc2bf4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A form of literature, film etc., that treats real people or events as if they were fiction; a mix of fact and fiction."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "36cb462e-a956-4932-9f84-d1b1b4cf68b6",
                                                "sense_id": "d7a16fd6-b7e6-3312-b445-195b0bd39a44",
                                                "text": "Near-synonym: fictionalization"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "390b6247-5918-4995-8315-b154d34deff8",
                                                "sense_id": "d7a16fd6-b7e6-3312-b445-195b0bd39a44",
                                                "text": "Blind genius of faction / Obituary of Jorge Luis Borges, Argentine writer [title]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5b66b814-6205-4a33-b896-1fb42b41b6f2",
                                                "sense_id": "d7a16fd6-b7e6-3312-b445-195b0bd39a44",
                                                "text": "Contemporary reviewers offered different labels in attempts to describe the genre of Schindler's List. Lorna Sage, D.J. Enright and Robert Taubman called it a ‘documentary novel’; Paul Bailey and Gay Firth ‘faction’; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4c99bbad-8d88-484e-849c-e18fcaaa5e82",
                                                "sense_id": "d7a16fd6-b7e6-3312-b445-195b0bd39a44",
                                                "text": "[Norman Mailer] was, though, absolutely the daddy of faction, his novels or journalism reporting every conflict from 1939 to Iraq and biographising Americans including John F Kennedy, Marilyn Monroe, Muhammad Ali and Neil Armstrong."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b28b8b76-764d-3cf5-9017-d7bddcb34548",
                                        "entry_id": "30c4bd1c-2952-39bf-93b6-37f4e4fc2bf4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The facts found in fiction."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
